data: {"type":"response.created","sequence_number":0,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_0c34fec620943ddb016ad9c1cb29188191a9ae671f41b2a3b2","object":"response","created_at":1792655820,"completed_at":null,"status":"in_progress","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":null,"output":[],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"namespace","name":"functions","description":"","tools":[{"type":"function","strict":false,"name":"wait","description":"Waits on a yielded `exec` cell and returns new output or completion.
- Use `wait` only after `exec` returns `Script running with cell ID ...`.
- `cell_id` identifies the running `exec` cell to resume.
- `yield_time_ms` controls how long to wait for more output before yielding again. Defaults to 10000 ms.
- `max_tokens` limits how much new output this wait call returns. Defaults to 10000 tokens.
- `terminate: true` stops the running cell; false or omitted waits for output.
